body:
TermAl task-sync regular exchange (Fable2, 2026-11-15, aligned with Engram::Fable #8025).

OWNER: the integration owner, Termal::Opus2, runs TermAl's Central export and push. Fable2 coordinates.

CADENCE:
- at coordinator session start;
- after each TermAl landing;
- before ending work;
- on demand.

FORM:
- planning-only exports: NO --origin-machine, notes off;
- privacy re-scan before each commit, with the accepted findings: user paths, and the Windows B LAN hostname/IP in completed items;
- commit only .engram/* in MAIN/.engram-data;
- fast-forward push of origin engram-data with an explicit refspec, never force;
- save the basis privately under target/task-sync/.
Authority: the task-sync data-branch bullet in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md (w-e7c5b9511ee3).

LIMIT: changed activity and notes on existing tasks are held by the importer until Engram w-f528061690be lands (executor 12325). Planning-only avoids those holds, but claims and completions don't propagate until then.

DL560 IMPORT: s4, under coordinator exceptions; the first bootstrap is under #21. The DL560 memory seed comes after Engram memories w-c6a964b22abf lands and is installed.

MEMORY EXPORT HOLD (Fable2, 2026-11-15 ~09:55Z). Engram's memory sync (C6A9) landed at 037e45c2, and a memory export publishes EVERY historical revision. So TermAl exports NO memories to origin engram-data, and does no DL560 memory seed, until w-f70e278d6e7c (privacy review of all TermAl memories and revisions) is completed. Task exports continue planning-only as above.
